  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Jacobs Engineering Group is obligated $274M in federal contracts for FY2026 to date. Jacobs Engineering Group won 147 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.9M, and obligations are up 194.6% year over year. Jacobs Engineering Group obligations rose from FY21 $33.4M, FY22 $27.5M, FY23 $52.6M, FY24 $64M, FY25 $93M to FY26 $274M. Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer for Jacobs Engineering Group at $151M, followed by Department of Defense at $36.6M and General Services Administration at $34.6M. Jacobs Engineering Group does most work in Engineering Services at $243M, with additional work in Architectural Services at $14.6M and Remediation Services at $9.4M. Jacobs Engineering Group also records activity with Department of Transportation at $33M, NASA at $9.9M, EPA at $9.2M, and other agencies in smaller amounts.",
    "sections": [
